  "note": "Annual election of the Antrim Town Commissioners, polled Friday 15 January 1926. Twelve candidates were nominated on 5 January for nine vacancies; Charles Burrowes, James Abernethy and H. Millar withdrew on 6 January, leaving nine for nine, so the nine were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1926, p. 10; 7 January 1926, p. 7). Burrowes, Abernethy and Millar withdrew; the remaining nine are named in the same report. Returned unopposed."
